course: dictionary
lesson: 2481
title: Daytime and night words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Daytime is the part of the day when it is light outside, between sunrise and sunset. You can use clues to work out what it means. «The nocturnal house swaps day and night: lights are dim in the zoo's daytime and bright at night.» Dim lights in the daytime and bright lights at night show that daytime is the light part of the day.
explain: Daytime can also come before another noun, to say that something happens during the day. Read «daytime TV» and «a daytime nap». Ask: could I say "during the day" instead? If yes, daytime is working as a describing word. Try your meaning in the sentence to check.
explain: Words that are opposites help too. Daytime is the opposite of night-time. In science, animals that are active in the daytime are called diurnal, and animals that are active at night are nocturnal. Knowing the opposite of a word can show you its meaning.
fact: Daytime means the part of the day when it is light, between sunrise and sunset.
fact: Daytime is usually not plural, so say «in the daytime», not «in the daytimes».
fact: Before another noun, daytime describes something that happens during the day, like «daytime TV».
fact: In science, animals active in the daytime are called diurnal, and the opposite is nocturnal.
fact: Phrases to learn: «in the daytime», «during the daytime», «daytime temperature».
exercise: «A boy in Texas woke his hamster in the daytime by poking it.» What does daytime mean in this sentence? | Only the early morning | *The part of the day when it is light outside | The part of the day when it is dark | A kind of hamster cage
exercise: Which phrase uses daytime to describe something that happens during the day? | a midnight feast | *a daytime nap | a dark cave | a starry sky
exercise: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt lead.» What does this tell you? | The surface is made of ice | The surface is freezing all day long | *The surface is very hot during its daytime | The surface is always covered in clouds
test: What is the opposite of daytime? | *Night-time | Morning | Lunchtime
test: Which word means active in the daytime? | atmosphere | *diurnal | nocturnal | constellation
exam: Which sentence uses daytime as a describing word? | *Daytime TV is boring, so I read a book | Mercury's daytime is very hot | Bats often sleep in the daytime | I like the daytime best
